<main>
  <h1>kyc.demo.kiosk.tech</h1>
  <p><strong>An anonymizing KYC broker.</strong></p>
  <p>
    This broker sits between the many government age and driving-licence services
    and the many operators that need to gate a regulated action. The human
    answers each check afresh, with nothing ticked in advance, and the broker
    keeps no earlier answer. For each check it returns to the requesting operator a
    <strong>signed, anonymized, single-use</strong> claim — "over 18",
    "holds a category-A licence" — and <strong>nothing that identifies the
    person</strong>: not the name, date of birth, or licence number.
  </p>
  <p>
    Each operator trusts the broker as an issuer once and asks for exactly the
    facts it needs. The operator never registers with a government identity
    service — the broker does that, once, for everyone.
  </p>

  <p class="stub">
    <strong>Demo stub — this does not check anything yet.</strong> On the
    verification page you simply <em>self-assert</em> the facts (you click
    yes/no); the broker takes your word for it. The <strong>real</strong> broker
    verifies that you <strong>hold a government account</strong>: for each check
    you log into a national eID or a mobile driving licence (mDL) and let the
    broker read your date of birth and licence category. It proves that the
    human holds such an account. It does <strong>not</strong> prove that the
    account belongs to the person who uses it, so one person can confirm facts
    for another. This demo proves the <em>protocol</em>: each request is bound
    to one operator, is used once, is answered on its own, and comes back as a
    signed answer that names nobody. It does <strong>not</strong> prove that the
    human is actually over 18, and it makes no liveness claim.
  </p>

  <p class="stub">
    <strong>Not a Kiosk operator.</strong> This broker signs facts about a
    person for operators. An assistant has nothing to call here, and the broker
    publishes no Kiosk discovery document. This is a page for a human, reached
    from a link your assistant relays to you.
  </p>

  <p class="stub">
    Verifications in flight: <%= @pending %> pending, <%= @confirmed %> confirmed.
    The verification page is reached only from an operator-issued link.
  </p>
</main>
